A 2010 meta-analysis by the US Department of Education found students in online conditions performed, on average, better than those receiving face-to-face instruction (effect size +0.24 standard deviations).
MIT OpenCourseWare and Coursera platform data show completion rates for motivated, self-selected learners of 60–80% — comparable to university dropout rates.
Medical students trained with virtual patient simulations perform equivalently to those with traditional clinical instruction on licensing exams, suggesting procedural learning transfers online.
